Subject: [PATCH] Fix draft model proposer position OOB crash when context exceeds draft model limit

When the target model supports a larger context (e.g. 128K) than the draft model
(e.g. Qwen3-0.6B with max_position_embeddings=40960), requests with long context
cause an out-of-bounds crash in the Ascend CANN gather_v3 operator during position
embedding lookup.

Root cause: position IDs >= draft_model.max_model_len are passed directly to the
draft model's embedding layer which only supports [0, max_model_len).

Fix: Use draft_max_model_len (not target max_model_len) for all position clamping
in DraftModelProposer. For the initial prefill pass, clamp positions exceeding the
draft model's limit to 0 and mask corresponding slot_mapping entries with
PADDING_SLOT_ID so the KV cache is not inadvertently written. seq_lens is computed
from original (unclamped) positions so attention correctness is preserved. Draft
tokens produced for over-limit positions will be garbage and rejected by the target
model's verification step, but the service will not crash.
---
Index: vllm_ascend/spec_decode/draft_model_proposer.py
===================================================================
diff --git a/vllm_ascend/spec_decode/draft_model_proposer.py b/vllm_ascend/spec_decode/draft_model_proposer.py
--- a/vllm_ascend/spec_decode/draft_model_proposer.py
+++ b/vllm_ascend/spec_decode/draft_model_proposer.py
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@
         self.runner = runner
 
         self.max_model_len = vllm_config.model_config.max_model_len
+        self.draft_max_model_len = vllm_config.speculative_config.draft_model_config.max_model_len
         max_batch_size = vllm_config.scheduler_config.max_num_seqs
         self.max_num_tokens = (self.vllm_config.scheduler_config.max_num_batched_tokens + max_batch_size)
 
@@ -261,7 +262,7 @@
             inputs=inputs,
             next_token_ids=next_token_ids,
             block_size=self.block_size,
-            max_model_len=self.vllm_config.model_config.max_model_len,
+            max_model_len=self.draft_max_model_len,
             arange=self.arange,
             cu_num_tokens=cu_num_tokens,
             num_reqs=self.runner.input_batch.num_reqs))
@@ -433,6 +434,14 @@
         # Shift the input ids by one token.
         self.input_ids[:num_tokens] = target_token_ids
         seq_lens = (target_positions[last_token_indices] + 1).int()
+        # Clamp positions to draft model's limit to prevent OOB in position embeddings.
+        # seq_lens is computed from original positions (needed for attention correctness).
+        _exceeds_draft = target_positions >= self.draft_max_model_len
+        if _exceeds_draft.any():
+            target_positions = target_positions.clone()
+            target_positions[_exceeds_draft] = 0
+            target_slot_mapping = target_slot_mapping.masked_fill(
+                _exceeds_draft.to(target_slot_mapping.device), PADDING_SLOT_ID)
 
         query_lens = cu_num_tokens[1:] - cu_num_tokens[:-1]
         max_query_len = query_lens.max().item()
@@ -542,7 +551,7 @@
             input_ids = draft_token_ids_tensor[now_speculative].to(device)
             positions_cpu += 1
 
-            exceeds_max_model_len = positions_cpu >= self.vllm_config.model_config.max_model_len
+            exceeds_max_model_len = positions_cpu >= self.draft_max_model_len
             # Mask out the position ids that exceed the max model length.
             # Otherwise, we may get out-of-range error in RoPE.
             clamped_positions_cpu = torch.where(exceeds_max_model_len, 0, positions_cpu)
